  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is our best result at 61.9% acc, showing that multiprofile with avgpool aggregation drives the largest gain (+9.2% over singleprofile). However, we have only tested one aggregation strategy (avgpool) in the multiprofile setting. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) that can model inter-profile interactions would outperform the simple mean-pooling, or whether avgpool is already near-optimal for this task. This experiment (config_020) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat fusion, multiprofile) constant relative to config_018, making it a clean single-variable test. Under the limited budget, resolving whether transformer aggregation adds value over avgpool is critical: if it helps, it opens a new optimization axis; if it does not, we can rule it out and redirect effort toward fusion strategy or image encoder choice. This is the highest-information-per-experiment next step."
}

